-- Generated by hyprlang2lua. Review TODOs before reloading Hyprland.

-- Display layout FIRST. Everything below draws onto whatever outputs
-- exist, so the outputs have to be right before anything paints.
-- Replaces kanshi -- see conf/monitors.sh for why.

-- BUG-2. Nothing owned org.freedesktop.Notifications: the name was only
-- registered for D-Bus ACTIVATION by org.kde.plasma.Notifications.service,
-- whose Exec is `plasma_waitforname`, which blocks until plasmashell
-- appears -- and under Hyprland it never does. So notify-send did not
-- fail, it hung forever, wedging every script that reported status.
-- dunst was installed and simply never started; it claims the name
-- directly, so the Plasma activation entry can no longer fire.
-- Must come before the bar, whose readings can notify on first poll.

-- BLUETOOTH TOASTS ARE OFF, deliberately. bt-notify.sh announced every
-- connect and disconnect, and it did so from a 3s poll -- so the toast
-- arrived after the thing it was announcing was already visible, and it
-- was announcing something the Bluetooth panel and the bar icon both
-- show anyway. Two surfaces saying the same thing, one of them late.
-- The script is still on disk; putting the line back is all it takes.
--
-- Nothing replaces it: the island's Bluetooth panel and glyph bind BlueZ
-- natively (quickshell/Bt.qml) and say what failed inside the row it
-- failed in. bt-watch.sh, which repainted eww's panel from BlueZ
-- signals, was deleted with that panel on 2026-09-16.

-- Same idea for PipeWire: one `pactl subscribe` pushes the volume, the
-- mute and the mic into eww and signals the bar, so the slider readout
-- and the bar glyph move with the volume instead of on a 1s timer. The
-- defpolls in eww.yuck and the interval on custom/volume are what is
-- left of the old polling, and they are a safety net now -- if this is
-- not running, audio goes stale-but-not-broken, which is the symptom to
-- recognise.

-- The battery notifier stays: nothing on the bar shows charge, so this
-- is the only thing that can speak up.

-- Warm the launcher's app index at login. The Search panel rebuilds it on open
-- whenever an application directory has changed, so this is not required
-- for correctness -- it moves the ~240ms scan of every .desktop file off
-- the first Super+S of the session, which is the one time you would
-- notice it.

-- ── The net under the popups ─────────────────────────────────────────
-- An eww popup is a layer surface; the backdrop is a full-screen one and
-- the launcher's keyboard twin takes the pointer and the keyboard
-- exclusively. Left behind, either one makes the whole desktop stop
-- responding to the mouse while showing nothing at all -- which reads as
-- "the browser froze", not as "a popup is stuck".
--
-- panel.sh's lock is what stops that happening. This notices if it does
-- anyway (eww 0.5.0 can leak a surface its own registry no longer lists,
-- and then no script can close it) and clears it within ~4s. Read the
-- note at the top of the script for the two faults it looks for.

-- ── THE BAR IS QUICKSHELL NOW ────────────────────────────────────────
-- waybar's line used to be here and is gone rather than commented out;
-- the command is in git and in architecture.md. What replaced it draws
-- the same island and calls the same scripts -- Actions.qml is the whole
-- seam -- so eww keeps all five panels and dunst, rofi and wlogout never
-- learn anything changed.
--
-- TWO THINGS DID CHANGE, and both are worth knowing before you wonder:
--
--   * The exclusive zone is 38, not 50. The island hangs off the top
--     edge instead of sitting 12 px below it, so every window on the
--     desktop starts 12 px higher. general.lua's gap note is updated.
--   * THE SYSTEM TRAY WENT WITH WAYBAR. waybar owned
--     org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher; nothing has claimed it since. It
--     was registered and EMPTY at handover -- zero items -- so nothing
--     on this desktop lost an icon, but the next app that wants one
--     will not find a host. Quickshell 0.3.1 does ship
--     Quickshell.Services.SystemTray; the island simply has no tray in
--     it yet. → open-items.md
--
-- To put waybar back for a side-by-side, start it by hand; the two bars
-- coexist fine, waybar just draws 12 px lower.

hl.on("hyprland.start", function()
    hl.exec_cmd("dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE")
    hl.exec_cmd("~/.config/hypr/conf/monitors.sh daemon")
    hl.exec_cmd("dunst")
    hl.exec_cmd("quickshell -p ~/.config/quickshell/shell.qml")
    hl.exec_cmd("hyprpaper")
    hl.exec_cmd("/usr/bin/kwalletd6 --replace")
    hl.exec_cmd("~/.config/hypr/conf/startup.sh")
    hl.exec_cmd("~/.config/eww/scripts/batt-notify.sh")
    hl.exec_cmd("python3 ~/.config/eww/scripts/apps.py refresh")
    hl.exec_cmd("~/.config/eww/scripts/eww-watchdog.sh")
end)

